{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs7FQZVceXr4yhPjL867","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Root cause:** `reporting/dedupe.py` kept `seen_ids` as a list, so every `event_id in seen_ids` check scanned the whole list. That makes deduplication quadratic in the number of rows. The refactor was meant to preserve first-occurrence order, and it did, but it dropped the set lookup.\n\n**Fix:** `seen_ids` is now a `set`. The output list is still built in first-occurrence order, so the output and the public API are unchanged.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_perf.py` with three tests:\n- An order-preservation test.\n- A timing test that dedupes 60k rows and must finish in under 1 second.\n- A `build_report` test on 40k rows that must finish in under 2 seconds.\n\nWith the old code, the two timing tests fail (the dedupe one took about 6 seconds). With the fix, the full suite passes (4 tests in 0.09s).\n\nThe two timing thresholds are wall-clock, so they could be flaky on a heavily loaded machine. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2195,"cache_read_input_tokens":29593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2195},"output_tokens":343,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e2f4172-e73a-4e65-8376-a38fc12df9ac","uuid":"379b5479-3b6b-46a5-b866-83879823b7f2","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:07:07.070Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs7FPjtD4MAvjnB7cNxA"}
